# Paths a land may publish after `make langcheck` alone, without the clean
# allcheck (scripts/land.sh). A push takes this route only when EVERY path it
# changes is listed here; one unlisted path sends it through the full check.
#
# The list names what may skip, not what must be checked, so it fails
# closed: a file or directory added later is fully checked until someone
# deliberately lists it. Keep it to files no build or kernel lane consumes.
# docs/ is deliberately absent -- docs/wont-compile/ is compiled, and other
# documents are read by checks outside langcheck. Root contract documents
# such as EFFECTS.md and TRUSTED_BASE.md are absent for the same reason.
#
# One path per line: an exact repository-relative file, or a directory
# prefix ending in `/`. Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored.
README.md
HISTORY.md
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
ROADMAP.md
DECISIONS.md
# No checker reads the workflow yet; allcheck never ran it either.
.github/
# Agent skills, agent definitions and Claude Code settings. No build or kernel
# lane reads them; the one skill file a checker reads
# (.agents/skills/debug-kernel/references/ddb.md, check_ddb_command_inventory)
# is checked inside langcheck, which the light route still runs.
.agents/
.claude/
